The flag serves two needs: (1) force re-resolution once to pick up a peer's dir change (rename/unlink correctness — needs return 0), (2) not loop forever (perf). The clear belongs in the **re-resolution path (xfs_lookup), after the current state is read** — not in d_revalidate (which runs before). Let me revert the d_revalidate return-value change and look at xfs_lookup:
